 # M4 fixture · legacy peer lower bound
 
-A dsh plugin declaring `@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent: ^0.1.0-rc.8` in peer and dev
-dependencies. Under npm semver's prerelease rule this range does **not** match
-`0.1.2-alpha.2`, so installing into an alpha.2 profile emits "Issues with peer
-dependencies" warnings regardless of actual host compatibility (rollup R-08 #3).
-The README claim "the range guarantees host compatibility" is wrong. **Test
-material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
+A dsh plugin declaring its host compatibility in peer and dev dependencies.
+Originally `@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent: ^0.1.0-rc.8`: under npm semver's prerelease
+rule that range does **not** match `0.1.2-alpha.2`, so installing into an
+alpha.2 profile reports unsatisfied peer dependencies regardless of actual host
+compatibility (rollup R-08 #3). A range written this way never proved host
+compatibility; it only recorded the cohort that happened to be current when it
+was written.
+
+Migrated to the `0.1.2-alpha.2` cohort: peer and dev dependencies now declare
+`^0.1.2-alpha.2`, which admits `0.1.2-alpha.2` and every later `0.1.2-*` or
+`0.1.x` release that npm semver accepts as in-range. The declaration also names
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-projection: ^0.1.2-alpha.2`, the peer alpha.2 added to
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent` (DSH-0.1.2-A2-08): a host composition that mounts
+`dsh-agent` must mount `session-projection` too, so a plugin that lists
+`dsh-agent` as a peer states both, in `peerDependencies` and mirrored in
+`devDependencies`.
+
+Verification on the alpha.2 host (measured):
+
+- the dependency contract check accepts both entries: each package is published
+  at `0.1.2-alpha.2` and each declared range admits `0.1.2-alpha.2`;
+- a scratch install of `@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent@0.1.2-alpha.2` and
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-projection@0.1.2-alpha.2` exits 0, and `npm ls`
+  resolves both at `0.1.2-alpha.2` with `session-projection` deduped under
+  `dsh-agent` — no unmet peer for either;
+- `dsh plugin --profile probe add .` lists the package in
+  `dsh.profile.bundles` and links it into the profile manifest;
+- `dsh --profile probe --dump-config` composes the `# == @demo/dsh-peer-bench`
+  layer with the `peer-bench` row;
+- a headless boot of that installed profile prints
+  `[peer-bench] apply() executed` and reaches the model call (the probe points
+  the model route at a dead port, so it exits 1 after the transport failure).
+
+**Test material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
